    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d643-a1">

                <pb facs="0631" n="533" sameAs="frus:frus1900/pg533"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Messrs. Norton &amp; Son to
                        Mr. Geldart</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >New York</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1899-12-14"><hi rendition="#italic">December 14,
                        1899</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#center">[Copy of letter received this a.m. from Norton &amp; Son,
                    Produce Exchange, New York.]</p>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">s. s. beatrice.</hi></p>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Sir</hi>: We beg to advise you that we are just
                    informed that this steamer has discharged all of her Delagoa Bay cargo into
                    lighters at East London, under orders of the British Government, and in
                    accordance with the terms and conditions of the American and African bill of
                    lading, clause 1, the steamship line is relieved of any further responsibility,
                    and goods are at risk and expense of consignees after leaving ship’s side.</p>
                <p>Yours, very truly,</p>
                <closer><hi rendition="#small-caps">Norton &amp; Son.</hi></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
